invariant: INV-59
file: mldsa.c
catches: test/wycheproof.sh
reason: the call takes a context of 256 bytes or more, which FIPS 204
  Algorithm 3 refuses. Its length byte wraps to 0, so a signature made
  with that byte verifies, and Wycheproof's case of a 256-byte context
  signed with length byte 0 must fail.

--- old
    if (pk_len != MLDSA87_PK_LEN || sig_len != MLDSA87_SIG_LEN || ctx_len > MLDSA_CONTEXT_MAX) {
--- new
    if (pk_len != MLDSA87_PK_LEN || sig_len != MLDSA87_SIG_LEN) {
